  "body": "## What changed (test only)\n\nSince #140 marches lateral rapids, the march subsumes `Rest::hidden_along` for a flat tool on a straight rapid, so deleting the `hidden_along` call in `crates/sim/src/verify/rapids.rs` left every `overhang_laws` test green (#206, from the review of PR #205).\n\nNew pair in `crates/sim/tests/overhang_laws.rs`, with a ball r6 stated as the judged cutter:\n\n- a floor pass along X 21 (disc X [15, 27], stopping at the ledge's edge), a pass at Z 12 along X 15 (columns X [9, 21] cleared to the ledge top; nothing under the ledge cleared - a chord clears hidden stock only from its own plane up), then a lateral rapid at Z 9.5 along X 20.5;\n- its footprint reaches X 14.51; only the march's rim ring stands over X < 15.26, judged at the 7th ring's lift (3.08) - 12.58 over columns at 12, so the march acquits;\n- the hidden-stock arm reads the disc at the tip plane, through the uncut band X [14.51, 15) under the ledge (X (5, 15], Z [10, 12]), and convicts.\n\n## Readings\n\n- With the ledge: `RapidInStock { at: 6 }`.\n- Same moves beside the bare post: no `RapidInStock` - the conviction is the hidden-stock arm's alone.\n- **Mutation check:** with `let bad = marched;` in place of the `hidden_along` call, `a_ball_rim_the_march_lifts_clear_is_still_convicted_through_hidden_stock` fails and the other 12 `overhang_laws` tests pass - the gap #206 names, now closed.\n\nNote: for a ball the arm's tip-plane reading is conservative (the rim actually stands above the hidden band here); the test pins the arm, and its doc says so.\n\n## Gate\n\n`cargo test -p camcraft-sim --test overhang_laws`: 13 passed. `cargo clippy -p camcraft-sim --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `overhang_laws::a_ball_rim_the_march_lifts_clear_is_still_convicted_through_hidden_stock`\n- `overhang_laws::the_same_ball_rapid_beside_a_bare_post_is_clean`\n\nChangelog: none\n\nOutside contributor PR (fork).\n\nFixes #206\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
